I believe the current definition of fighting words is 1) the language
must be delivered one-to-one, and 2) must be such as to evoke an
immediate breach of peace (as opposed to simply offending the
listener). Vulgarities in an open forum are not fighting works; quite
the opposite they are constitutionally protected.

The University of Wisconsin tried to punish a student for email that
it called "fighting words". The federal district judge said that it's
rule against what-it-called-fighting-words was an illegal suppression
of the student's free speech right.

- Carl

